WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.390
The blob's code is two numbers:

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.250
where its brightness sits.

3
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.390
Decoding paints a blob there, and

4
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.030
it does not keep every pixel.

5
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.120
Today: squeeze a picture into a short

6
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.640
code, and what a nudge invents.

7
00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.590
Encoding finds the centre

8
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.270
of the brightness.

9
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.770
Decoding paints a new blob at that code.

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.860
Leave the code and the decode is close.

11
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.010
Move it and you invent a new blob,

12
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.410
not a repair of the old pixels.

13
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.470
Two numbers are a summary

14
00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.350
of this brightness.

15
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.780
They are not a map of meaning, and

16
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.040
they are not a photograph.

17
00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.410
Here the two numbers pick a place.

18
00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:47.630
The painted blob follows them, and the

19
00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.650
original pixels do not come back.

20
00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:51.390
Quick check!

21
00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.490
The two-number code of the

22
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.130
blob is which of these?

23
00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.970
Where the brightness sits.

24
00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.830
The exact pixels were never stored.

25
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.210
In the app, open the code lab.

26
00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.580
Leave the sliders, then move one, and say

27
00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.880
when the decode stopped being a rebuild.

28
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:12.990
Your turn.

29
00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.290
Does nudging the code repair

30
00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:17.490
the original pixels?

31
00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:19.690
Remember this.

32
00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.670
A short code rebuilds a summary.

33
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.390
A moved code is a new picture.

34
00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:27.450
Try it tonight.

35
00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:30.370
Write the two numbers of the original

36
00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:33.530
blob, then the difference after one nudge.
